{c: Chords from the writer's own lead sheet (MusicXML in the source above)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]O Lord, my God, in you [G]alone I trust,
[D/F#]For you [Em7]have been my re[Bm7]fuge all my days.
[D]And even though the E[G]nemy will come,
[D/F#]You res[Em7]cue me and com[Bm7]fort me always.
[Bm7]Who [A/C#]is [D]like [Dadd2/F#]our God?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[A]As for [G]me, I will al[D]ways hope in You.
I will lift [Bm7]my praise to You, more and more.
[A]As for [G]me, I will shout [D]with joy to You.
As I sing [Bm7]my praise to You, more and more.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]My lips will tell Your deeds [G]so marvelous,
[D/F#]Your power [Em7]and righteousness [Bm7]and Yours alone.
[D]Your mighty works I'll share [G]with those to come,
[D/F#]Though I [Em7]may not know how [Bm7]to share them all.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge}
[D]Though I've seen trou[D/F#]bles, [Gmaj7]many and bitter,
[Bm]You will restore my [Asus]life a[G]gain.
[D]In all my struggles, [Gmaj7]You have delivered,
[Bm]You will restore my [Asus]life a[G]gain.
[D]Though I've seen trou[D/F#]bles, [Gmaj7]many and bitter,
[Bm]You will restore my [Asus]life a[G]gain.
[D]In all my struggles, [Em9]You have delivered,
[Bm/F#]You will restore my life a[G]gain,
And again!
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus 2}
[A]As for [G]me, I will al[D]ways hope in You.
I will lift [Bm]my praise to You, more and more.
[A]As for [G]me, I will shout [D]with joy to You.
As I sing [Bm]my praise to You, more and more.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Tag}
[Bm7]Who [A/C#]is [D]like [Dadd2/F#]our God?
{end_of_verse}
